-- title:
--   Uniform mask, workspace, and word budgets satisfy every reporting-level scratch contract
-- statement:
--   Let $h,J,N_B,N_C,g$ and all addresses and indices be natural numbers, and put $W=512hJ$. Choose a level $k\le\lfloor13J/20\rfloor$. Let $D$ be the retained level catalog selected by report-bank base $r$, occurrence index $s$, band indices $i,j$, and level $k$; its two source sizes are the cardinalities of those bands. Define
--   $$\begin{aligned}
--   A&=2^W,& B&=(W+1)^2+8(W+1)+8,\\
--   L_W(N)&=4\cdot2^{2W}(N+1)+4(N+1)+N+2^{2W+2}+2^{W+1}+16,\\
--   C&=(W+1)2^{W+1}+L_W(2^{2W})+(2^W+1)2^W(2^Wg)^2.
--   \end{aligned}$$
--   If mask base $a$, workspace base $b$, and machine limits $S,M$ satisfy $a+A\le b$, $b+B\le S$, and $C\le M$, then
--   $$\operatorname{Scratch}(D,k,|B_i|,|C_j|,a,b;S,M).$$
--   This contract comprises mask capacity; Pascal, power-table, and remainder workspace; lookup and query word bounds; and the required switch/cut inequalities.
--
--   Thus one fixed allocation suffices for every prescribed reporting level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/SharedReportingBankResourceBoundsQuery.lean#L77-L128

